From: Adrien Girardeau <adrigir25@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:37:35 +0100
Subject: malloc_extend_top without a cast as lvalue

Store sbrk_base through its word, not through a cast.

malloc_extend_top set sbrk_base through the macro's cast, ((char *)D_0012FBA0[0]) = brk: a GCC
extension (a cast as lvalue) that Clang refuses, so hostgen.json skipped the whole file and the
port had no C for it. A build without the disc then ran it as a stub, and newlib's _malloc_r (the
game's sprintf of a float, through _dtoa_r and _Balloc) got no memory from it. D_0012FBA0 is a u32
and a pointer is 32 bits on the EE: the store is the same, and EE-GCC 2.96 compiles both into the
same code.
---
 src/sdk/libc/malloc/malloc_extend_top.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sdk/libc/malloc/malloc_extend_top.c b/src/sdk/libc/malloc/malloc_extend_top.c
index e9b768f3..d2644b05 100644
--- a/src/sdk/libc/malloc/malloc_extend_top.c
+++ b/src/sdk/libc/malloc/malloc_extend_top.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ void malloc_extend_top(struct _reent *reent_context, u32 nb) {
         set_head(top, top_size | PREV_INUSE);
     } else {
         if (sbrk_base == (char *)(-1))
-            sbrk_base = brk;
+            D_0012FBA0[0] = (u32)brk; /* sbrk_base = brk */
         else
             sbrked_mem += brk - (char *)old_end;
 
